e another integration choice. Standard transports are stdio and Streamable HTTP. The HTTP authorization specification applies to protected HTTP servers; local stdio credentials are managed separately."," ",(0,t.jsx)("a",{href:"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/architecture",children:"MCP architecture"}),","," ",(0,t.jsx)("a",{href:"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports",children:"transports"})," and"," ",(0,t.jsx)("a",{href:"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/authorization",children:"authorization"}),"."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:[(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Runtime and context."})," Model inference, tool execution and stored run history are separate concerns. Checkpoints support recovery; selected context controls what enters each model call. Completion, cancellation and step or time limits bound the run. Retrieval and long-term memory are optional and do not require a vector database. Sandboxes and specialist agents depend on the task."," ",(0,t.jsx)("a",{href:"https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/managed-agents",children:"Runtime separation"}),","," ",(0,t.jsx)("a",{href:"https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-context-engineering-for-ai-agents",children:"context engineering"})," and"," ",(0,t.jsx)("a",{href:"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/persistence",children:"persistence"}),"."]}),(0,t.jsxs)("p",{children:[(0,t.jsx)("strong",{children:"Action controls."})," Tool results do not confer authority. Input validation, least-privilege access and policy-based approval govern execution. Generated code needs a constrained execution environment. Record redacted events and evaluate model, prompt and tool changes before release. Bound retries and use idempotency or deduplication so resuming work does not duplicate a business action."," ",(0,t.jsx)("a",{href:"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/server/tools#security-considerations",childr